# Reference only — copy to .env (gitignored) and fill in real values, never commit .env itself.
#
# IMPORTANT: this site is static (GitHub Pages, no server). SOUNDCLOUD_CLIENT_SECRET
# must NEVER be used in client-side JS or baked into a GitHub Actions build step —
# anything shipped to the browser is public, secret or not. It only belongs in a
# server-side context (e.g. a serverless proxy), which this project does not have.
#
# SOUNDCLOUD_CLIENT_ID is the one value that's safe to expose client-side (SoundCloud's
# own oEmbed/Widget embeds work without it; it's only needed if you later call the API
# directly for public-resource lookups via Client Credentials, done server-side).

SOUNDCLOUD_CLIENT_ID=
SOUNDCLOUD_CLIENT_SECRET=
